<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yadega</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Naaba Yadega</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yadega is the traditional founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mossi">Mossi</a> kingdom of Yatenga in the north of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burkina-faso">Burkina Faso</a>, usually dated to the first half of the 16th century. Mossi tradition says that he was a prince of the Ouagadougou royal line who, passed over in a succession dispute, went north with the royal regalia and founded his own kingdom. Later kings of Yatenga traced their descent from him.</p></div>
